  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Provision of Scientific Advice on food safety</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project supports the FAO provision of scientific advice process be convening expert meetings and collecting data on emerging issues of concern for food safety governance.  Specifically, this project will synthesize current and updated food safety related research on the following three topics: 1) food safety considerations on cellular agriculture application in meat, poultry, seafood, eggs and dairy products; 2) risk analysis of methyl-mercury in seafood; 3) application of whole genome sequencing (WGS) to address microbial hazards and antimicrobial resistance (AMR) in low and middle income countries; and 4) the overall support to the provision of scientific advice through JECFA, JEMRA, JEMNU, JMPR and other ad hoc expert meetings in the area of food safety.</narrative>
  </description>
